        <informationafterdive>
          <greatestdepth>10.0</greatestdepth>
          <averagedepth>9.274</averagedepth>
          <diveduration>2160</diveduration>
          <lowesttemperature>290.15</lowesttemperature>
          <notes>
            <para>4th and final PADI Open Water Diver dive. Me and my buddy planned out the route, picking a few spots to visit in the reservoir and how to navigate back. We already covered most of the skills in the previous dives so this was mostly just a fun &amp; chill exploration of the things we wanted to see. Even though the visibility wasn't great it was still really enjoyable!!

For completeness sake here's the PADI spec for the last dive, but fwiw it was mostly just a chill dive
- Briefing and dive planning
- Assemble, put on and adjust equipment
- Predive safety check
- Entry
- Weight and trim check, adjustment
- Five point free descent without reference
- Underwater exploration
- Ascent with safety stop
- Exit
- Debrief and log dive
- Post dive equipment care</para>
          </notes>
          <rating>
            <ratingvalue>8</ratingvalue>
          </rating>
          <visibility>3</visibility>
        </informationafterdive>
